    result: "r — the reaction rate, the number of moles of product formed (or reactant consumed) per liter per second at a given instant.",
    interpretation: "The rate law reveals the microscopic mechanism of a reaction: if doubling [A] quadruples the rate (m = 2), two molecules of A must collide in the slow step, giving chemists a direct window into the molecular choreography.",
